  <content>
  <section><para>Your teacher will assign you one of these expressions:</para>
<para>\( \dfrac {n^2 - 9}{2(4-3)}\qquad \text{or} \qquad (n+3)\cdot \dfrac {n-3}{8-3\cdot2} \)</para>
<para>For numbers 1 - 4, evaluate your expression when \(n\) is the given value.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Warm Up Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="79719b29-e056-4e5a-85b9-40c373225c3c"><problem><para>
      <para>\(n = 5\)</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>8</para><para>
      <para>Nice try! The correct answer is 8.</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
<!--Q#-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What did you discover when you compared your answers? Explain your rationale.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. 
      Even though our questions were different, the answers were the same because the expressions were equivalent.
    </para>
  </solution></exercise>
